#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:19
msgid ""
"``ros2 bag`` records data from topics, services, and actions so you can save "
"and replay it later. This tutorial shows you how to record, inspect, and "
"play back that data with the ``ros2 bag`` command-line tools. After "
"completing it, you can create bag files, examine their contents, and replay "
"them for debugging or analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:29
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:32
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:34
msgid ""
"Use ``ros2 bag record`` to save data from topics, services, and actions, "
"``ros2 bag info`` to inspect a recording, and ``ros2 bag play`` to replay "
"it. Recordings are stored in bag directories that you can share or reuse to "
"reproduce experiments. By default, recordings use the MCAP (``.mcap``) "
"storage format. Humble and earlier distributions use SQLite (``.db3``) by "
"default."
msgstr ""

