#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:357
msgid ""
"Playback lasts as long as the original recording, even if the turtle was not "
"moving for some of that time. This is because the ``subset`` bag also "
"recorded the ``/turtle1/pose`` topic, which was published throughout the "
"recording."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:360
msgid ""
"While the ``/turtlesim`` node is active, it publishes data on the ``/turtle1/"
"pose`` topic at regular intervals. In the ``ros2 bag info`` example above, "
"the ``/turtle1/cmd_vel`` topic ``Count`` is 9, matching the number of arrow-"
"key presses during recording."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:363
msgid ""
"The ``/turtle1/pose`` topic ``Count`` is over 3000 because data was "
"published on that topic throughout the recording."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:365
msgid "To see how often position data is published, run:"
