#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:385
msgid "$ ros2 bag record -o subset_cmd_vel --topics /turtle1/cmd_vel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:389
msgid "In another new terminal, from the ``bag_files`` directory, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:391
msgid "$ ros2 bag record -o subset_pose --topics /turtle1/pose"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:395
msgid "Move the turtle around, then stop both recordings with :kbd:`Ctrl-C`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:396
msgid ""
"To play these recordings together with correct timing, pass ``-i "
"<bag_name>`` for each bag:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:398
msgid "$ ros2 bag play -i subset_cmd_vel -i subset_pose"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:402
msgid ""
"This plays the ``subset_cmd_vel`` and ``subset_pose`` recordings together, "
"with playback synced to replicate the original message order. The optional "
"argument ``--message-order {received,sent}`` sets whether messages are "
"sequenced by receive time or publish time. The default is ``received``. This "
"option also applies when playing a single bag."
msgstr ""

