#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:878
msgid "What does ``ros2 bag`` record?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:879
msgid ""
"It can record data from topics, services, and actions in your ROS system. "
"You choose which interfaces to record with options such as ``--topics``, ``--"
"services``, and ``--actions``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:882
msgid "Where are recordings saved?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:883
msgid ""
"In a bag directory created in the working directory where you run ``ros2 bag "
"record``. Use ``-o`` to set a custom directory name. Each bag directory "
"contains metadata and the recorded data files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:887
msgid "How do I inspect a recording before playing it back?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:888
msgid ""
"Run ``ros2 bag info <bag_name>``. The output lists duration, message counts, "
"and which topics, services, and actions were recorded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:891
msgid "How do I play back service or action data?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data.rst:892
msgid ""
"For services, use ``ros2 bag play --publish-service-requests <bag_name>``. "
"For actions, use ``ros2 bag play --send-actions-as-client <bag_name>``. "
"Topic playback uses ``ros2 bag play <bag_name>``."
msgstr ""
